{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And HaShem's anger burned because he was going.</b> For He did not give him permission with a radiant countenance, as it is written, ״If to call you come etc.״ And he should have understood from the first time that it was not in the intent of HaShem that he go. And a parallel to this we find in the spies: ״Send for yourself men״ — yet it was revealed and known before Him that it was not in the intent of HaShem that they be sent. Another interpretation: <b>And HaShem's anger burned because he was going</b> — for He said, ״But only the matter that I speak to you — that you shall do,״ and Balaam should not have gone until he knew that matter; yet he hurried himself out of excessive hatred and did not wait for the speech. The pericope of Balaam was written to inform why HaShem removed the seven nations — for this one arose from among them and came to curse them without cause in their palms." "<b>And his two lads with him.</b> Only them — so that he would not have an opening to attribute the she-ass's deviation to the large retinue, to say she panicked because of the crowd. And despite this, he did not understand his way."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The abbreviation רה״ק is expanded as רוח הקודש (the holy spirit) based on context; ד״‎א = דבר אחר, another interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:20.250846278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}